# Esika's Chariot: "create a token that's a copy of target token you control". Both players cast a Chariot off four Moxen
# (Bot1 on turn 1, Bot2 on turn 2), so each controls two Cats. On turn 3 Bot1's Cats crew its Chariot and it attacks:
# the trigger's target question refuses Bot2's Cats (tokens, but not Bot1's) and takes one of Bot1's own (tapped from
# crewing, still a token it controls), so Bot1 ends with three Cats.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Esika's Chariot
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Esika's Chariot
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Esika's Chariot.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Esika's Chariot.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Esika's Chariot.Activate(Ability: Crew)
Bot1.Attack(Esika's Chariot > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Cat Token)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Cat Token)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cat Token#3.Power = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Cat Token#2.Power = 2
Bot2.Life = 16
